# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Mr. Chartist — Options Terminal | Environment Variables
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# ⚡ QUICK START: Just run `npm run dev` — no env vars needed!
#    The app works with TradingView + NSE data out of the box.
#    Add Upstox credentials below for premium real-time data.
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── UPSTOX BROKER API (Recommended — Primary Data Source) ──
# Sign up at https://upstox.com and create an app at:
# https://upstox.com/developer/api-documentation/open-api/
# Upstox provides: Real-time Option Chain, Greeks, Live LTP Feed, Historical Data
#
# Generate an OAuth access token via the Upstox login flow:
# https://upstox.com/developer/api-documentation/authentication/
#
# UPSTOX_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_upstox_oauth_access_token

# Optional: use Upstox sandbox instead of production API
# UPSTOX_SANDBOX=true

# ── PROXY DEBUG (Optional) ──
# Set PROXY_DEBUG=1 to print full error tracebacks and HTTP request logs to stderr.
# PROXY_DEBUG=1
# PROXY_DEBUG_VERBOSE=1
# Default: 4002. Change only if port 4002 is already in use.
# PROXY_PORT=4002

# ── MOBILE WEB PUSH (Optional — alerts when browser is closed) ──
# Generate keys:  npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
# Or:  python -c "from py_vapid import Vapid; v=Vapid(); v.generate_keys(); print(v.public_key); print(v.private_pem())"
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=your_public_key_base64url
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=your_private_key_base64url
# VAPID_CLAIMS_SUB=mailto:your@email.com

# ── VITE PROXY URL (Optional) ──
# Default: http://localhost:4002. Change only for custom proxy setups.
# Works with both Node.js (proxy-server.mjs) and Python (proxy_server) proxies.
# VITE_PROXY_URL=http://localhost:4002

# ── PYTHON PROXY (Optional alternative to Node.js proxy) ──
# Uses official upstox-python-sdk — https://upstox.com/developer/api-documentation/open-api
# Install: pip install -r requirements.txt
# Run standalone:  npm run proxy:python   OR   python -m proxy_server
# Run with frontend: npm run dev:python

# ── TA-LIB (Optional — Technical Analysis) ──
# https://ta-lib.org/ — RSI, MACD, Bollinger Bands, ADX, ATR, patterns
# Install C library first (see docs/TA-LIB.md), then: uv pip install TA-Lib numpy
# Endpoints: /api/ta/indicators, /api/ta/snapshot, /api/ta/scanner
# Charts also compute indicators client-side when proxy TA routes unavailable.
